<BaseLayout title="Writing — Ruijie Wu" description="Essays, notes and research at the crossings of embodiment, psychotherapy and culture.">
  <section class="page-intro container">
    <span class="eyebrow">Writing &amp; notes / 04</span>
    <h1>Thinking, feeling,<br /><em>making meaning.</em></h1>
    <p class="lede">A growing archive of questions, observations and research — not a catalogue of answers, but a place to follow ideas as they take shape.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="narrow">
      <span class="eyebrow">Themes I return to</span>
      <div class="writing-list">
        <article><span class="when">01 / Embodiment</span><div><h2>The body as a way of knowing</h2><p>Movement, sensation, body image and forms of knowledge that do not begin with words.</p></div></article>
        <article><span class="when">02 / Across cultures</span><div><h2>Living between worlds</h2><p>Migration, belonging, estrangement, identity and the emotional textures of cultural crossing.</p></div></article>
        <article><span class="when">03 / Psychotherapy</span><div><h2>Being human together</h2><p>Therapeutic relationships, trauma, grief, boundaries, care and the search for meaning.</p></div></article>
        <article><span class="when">04 / Movement</span><div><h2>Dance beyond performance</h2><p>What becomes possible when movement is approached as expression, exploration and relationship.</p></div></article>
        <article><span class="when">05 / Notes</span><div><h2>Fragments from everyday life</h2><p>Short reflections on culture, work, teaching and the small moments that open larger questions.</p></div></article>
      </div>
      <p class="writing-footnote">The themes above are an index of ongoing interests. Individual essays and publications will be added here as they are ready to share.</p>
